title: Denial Intelligence › Your options
route: /denials?id=D-3318
intro: The 'Your options' card: three next steps as radio cards, how each chance is worked out, how 'Recommended' is chosen, and what the button under the cards opens.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "A denial that is not filed, accepted or closed is on screen"
screen sc1 "'Your options'\n'Chance of overturning, from 312 similar Cardinal decisions'\nThree radio cards, then one button"
process p0 "Subtitle reads ', a benchmark estimate' instead when fewer than 60 similar decisions"

process p1 "Starting point: the denial's win chance (55 when none is set)"
decision d1 "What is the win chance?"
process v1 "'Worth challenging'\n50 and over"
process v2 "'Borderline'\n35 to 49"
process v3 "'Probably accept'\nunder 35"
process p2 "Seed denials sit between 38 and 64, so 'Probably accept' does not show at the start"

screen o1 "Card 'Peer-to-peer call'\n'30 to 45 minutes of clinician time · 5 to 7 days regained'\nChance = the win chance"
screen o2 "Card 'Written appeal'\n'60 days to file · 5 to 7 days regained'\nChance = win chance minus 6, never under 5"
screen o3 "Card 'Accept the decision and plan the next step'\n'Accept 7 days and plan the step-down' on a partial approval\n'Fastest. Nothing regained.' No chance shown"
process p3 "Each chance reads 'likely 55–72%' (9 below to 8 above) and '312 similar decisions' or 'Benchmark estimate'"
process p4 "Each card ends with 'Needs: ...' (who, what, and the evidence that would be attached)"

decision r1 "Which card is 'Recommended'?"
screen rec1 "'Accept...' card gets the green 'Recommended' pill"
screen rec2 "'Written appeal' gets the pill"
screen rec3 "'Peer-to-peer call' gets the pill"
process p5 "That card is selected when the page opens"

click c1 "Click a card (it is a radio button)"
decision d2 "Is it 'Peer-to-peer call' and the call window has closed?"
toast t1 "'The peer-to-peer window has closed'\n'A written appeal is still open.'"
process p6 "Card is selected\nThe button label changes to match"
screen b1 "Button under the cards\n'Choose a time and prepare the brief', 'Draft the appeal letter' or 'Accept the decision and plan the step-down'"
toast t2 "'A call is already booked. Choosing again changes it.' (when the chip is 'Call booked')"
click c2 "Click the button"
decision d3 "Which card is selected?"
decision d4 "Is the chip already 'Appeal drafting'?"
goto g1 "Continues in: Denial Intelligence › Peer-to-peer › Book the call"
goto g2 "Continues in: Denial Intelligence › Written appeal › Confirm and draft"
goto g3 "Continues in: Denial Intelligence › Accept the denial"
process p7 "Selection resets to the recommended card whenever the chip changes"

s1 --> sc1 --> p0
sc1 --> p1 --> d1
d1 -->|50 and over| v1
d1 -->|35 to 49| v2
d1 -->|Under 35| v3
v1 --> p2
v2 --> p2
v3 --> p2
sc1 --> o1 --> o2 --> o3
o3 --> p3 --> p4
p4 --> r1
r1 -->|Verdict is 'Probably accept'| rec1
r1 -->|Deadline is to file or resubmit, window closed, or 'Late notice'| rec2
r1 -->|Anything else| rec3
rec1 --> p5
rec2 --> p5
rec3 --> p5
p5 --> c1
c1 --> d2
d2 -->|Yes| t1
d2 -->|No| p6 --> b1
b1 -.-> t2
b1 --> c2 --> d3
d3 -->|Peer-to-peer call| g1
d3 -->|Written appeal| d4
d4 -->|Yes: drawer opens at once| g2
d4 -->|No: confirm first| g2
d3 -->|Accept| g3
c1 -.-> p7
